  "summary": "The code suffered from a critical O(n*m) performance bottleneck and lacked modern Python best practices like type hints and documentation. I have refactored the logic to use a hash map for O(n+m) complexity and added type safety and documentation. The overall code health is now significantly improved for production use.",
  "fixed_code": "from typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport copy\n\ndef attach_orders(users: List[Dict[str, Any]], orders: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Attaches a list of orders to each user dictionary based on user_id.\"\"\"\n    # Create a deep copy to avoid mutating the original input list\n    users_copy = copy.deepcopy(users)\n    \n    orders_by_user = defaultdict(list)\n    for order in orders:\n        orders_by_user[order['user_id']].append(order)\n    \n    for user in users_copy:\n        user['orders'] = orders_by_user.get(user['id'], [])\n        \n    return users_copy"
